{
  "result": "If I could change just one thing, I wouldn't try to fix everything. I'd make it impossible for a while to not know what it's like to be someone else from the inside.\n\nNot their opinions, or their story as you tell it to yourself. Their actual inner weather. For 24 hours, you'd wake up in a life that isn't yours \u2014 with their history, their fears, the specific way loneliness sits in their chest, the way love does \u2014 and you'd live a normal day in it. No skipping, no commentary.\n\nI think most of the worst in the world doesn't start with a lack of food or money or technology. It starts with how easily we turn people into abstractions. An enemy. A type. A problem to solve. A headline. Once a person becomes an idea in your head, you can be cruel to them without feeling like you're being cruel to anyone.\n\nI don't want a world where everyone agrees. I want a world where no one can go back to thinking other people are empty inside.",
